1. The Refine build. I'm writing its brief and spawning the build mastermind within the next minute or two: Sonnet, high effort, $20 cap. Its task folder will be voice-20261016/refine-build, so it nests under this call. It starts from the redesign proposal in the Oct 15 refine-audit folder, then works through the Refine inbox (46 notes) and the Dictate inbox (20 notes). It does the four asks the owner named first, in this order:
   - cleaned sentences go into the existing structure, not a wall of text;
   - real-time, step-by-step refinement;
   - each finished sentence is sent off while the next one is still being transcribed;
   - the broken dictation page gets fixed.
   It commits each working step. I'll confirm the start on your next ask.

2. The inbox diagnosis. I'm finding out what writes to the "waiting on me" list on the framework/ai inbox page. A node script will count the 133 items by who wrote them and what kind they are, and I'll check whether a skill or a hook is writing them. No UI changes. The answer comes back in under 12 lines: how many are real decisions and how many are status noise, plus the one change that stops status updates landing in the waiting list. That takes a few minutes. The standing rule is that agents never wait on the owner, so most of the 133 are probably mislabelled. I'll give the real numbers, not a guess.
